From 2c32e6d18f2d525cf932825a3d09f21b81e21a2f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lance <Gero3977@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 06:25:32 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 12/22] ASoC: codecs: wcd934x: ignore repeated MBHC micbias
 requests

wcd934x_mbhc_request_micbias() takes an MCLK vote on MICB_ENABLE and
drops one on MICB_DISABLE, but MBHC does not pair those calls. An unplug
while plug detection is running disables the micbias from both the
detection work and wcd_mbhc_report_plug_removal(). The second call drops
a vote nobody holds, which logs "ln_bb_clk1 already disabled" and takes
sysclk_users to -1.

That count then stays wrong. wcd934x_enable_ana_bias_and_sysclk() only
programs the hardware when ++sysclk_users == 1, so every later stream
skips the analog bias and MCLK setup. On the LG V30 the earpiece and WCD
headphone output then went silent with the DAPM path fully on, the PCM
running and no over-current interrupts, until the next reboot.

Ignore a request that repeats the current state, as the LG driver does.

Prior art and credits: micb_ena_status in tavil_mbhc_request_micbias(),
LG msm8998 kernel, sound/soc/codecs/wcd934x/wcd934x-mbhc.c. The Qualcomm
resource manager there also refuses to drop MCLK with no users.

TEST ONLY until the silence is shown gone on hardware.

Signed-off-by: Lance <Gero3977@gmail.com>
Assisted-by: Claude-Code:claude-opus-5-5
---
 sound/soc/codecs/wcd934x.c | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/sound/soc/codecs/wcd934x.c b/sound/soc/codecs/wcd934x.c
index 69f0ae2ca..ee58915bc 100644
--- a/sound/soc/codecs/wcd934x.c
+++ b/sound/soc/codecs/wcd934x.c
@@ -545,6 +545,7 @@ struct wcd934x_codec {
 	int dmic_sample_rate;
 	int comp_enabled[COMPANDER_MAX];
 	int sysclk_users;
+	bool mbhc_micb_on;
 	struct mutex sysclk_mutex;
 	/* mbhc module */
 	struct wcd_mbhc *mbhc;
@@ -2481,6 +2482,13 @@ static int wcd934x_mbhc_request_micbias(struct snd_soc_component *component,
 	struct wcd934x_codec *wcd = dev_get_drvdata(component->dev);
 	int ret;
 
+	/* MBHC can repeat a request; only a real change moves the MCLK vote */
+	if (req == MICB_ENABLE || req == MICB_DISABLE) {
+		if (wcd->mbhc_micb_on == (req == MICB_ENABLE))
+			return 0;
+		wcd->mbhc_micb_on = req == MICB_ENABLE;
+	}
+
 	if (req == MICB_ENABLE)
 		__wcd934x_cdc_mclk_enable(wcd, true);
 
